      "explanation": "Main idea: borgen can mean both borrow and lend, and the direction is determined by the sentence. borgen can mean both to borrow and to lend. Direction becomes clear by person and dative. If I take something from another, in English it is to borrow. If I give someone else time, in English it is to lend. In everyday life, leihen is also often used with a very similar meaning. Therefore, borgen must be read in context.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Kann ich mir dein Fahrrad borgen?",
          "lv": "Can i borrow your bike"
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich borge dir mein Buch.",
          "lv": "I lend you my book."
        },
        {
          "de": "Er borgt sich Geld von seinem Bruder.",
          "lv": "He borrows money from his brother."
        },
        {
          "de": "Sie borgt ihrer Freundin ein Kleid.",
          "lv": "She lends her friend a dress."
        },
        {
          "de": "Darf ich mir einen Stift borgen?",
          "lv": "Can i borrow a pen"
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir borgen den Nachbarn die Leiter.",
          "lv": "We lend neighbours ladders."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "borgen",
          "meaning": "Borrow / lend",
          "example": "Ich borge mir Geld. = Es aizņemos naudu."
        },
        {
          "word": "leihen",
          "meaning": "Lend / borrow",
          "example": "Kannst du mir das Buch leihen? = Vai vari man aizdot grāmatu?"
        },
        {
          "word": "geben",
          "meaning": "To give",
          "example": "Ich gebe dir Geld. = Es tev dodu naudu."
        },
        {
          "word": "zurückgeben",
          "meaning": "Give back",
          "example": "Ich gebe das Buch zurück. = Es atdodu grāmatu."
        }
      ],
      "tip": {
        "leftBlocks": [
          {
            "text": "mir borgen often means to borrow for oneself."
          },
          {
            "text": "dir/ihm borgen often means to lend to another."
          }
        ]
      },
      "important": {
        "text": "the meaning of borgen depends on the direction.",
        "example": "Ich borge mir etwas = I borrow. Ich borge dir etwas = I lend you."
      },
