      "id": "a2-folgen",
      "layout": "standardStudy",
      "translation": "To follow",
      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: folgen means to follow someone or something, but a result can also follow from the situation.",
        "When it comes to a person, a way, or an instruction, folgen usually means to follow.",
        "The phrase jemandem folgen is often used, where the German is dative.",
        "If something follows logically from what has been said before, folgen can mean to follow.",
        "Folgen is not a root word meaning listen or obey • Gehorchen is more commonly used for this.",
        "At A2 level, the most important meanings are follow and follow."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Folgen Sie mir bitte.",
          "lv": "Please follow me"
        },
        {
          "de": "Der Hund folgt dem Kind.",
          "lv": "The dog follows the child."
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich folge deinem Rat.",
          "lv": "I followed your advice."
        },
        {
          "de": "Bitte folgen Sie den Anweisungen.",
          "lv": "Please follow the instructions."
        },
        {
          "de": "Aus diesen Zahlen folgt ein Problem.",
          "lv": "A problem arises from these numbers."
        },
        {
          "de": "Das Kind gehorcht den Eltern.",
          "lv": "The child listens to the parents."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "folgen",
          "meaning": "Follow / follow",
          "example": "Ich folge dir. = Es tev sekoju."
        },
        {
          "word": "verfolgen",
          "meaning": "Pursue / follow",
          "example": "Die Polizei verfolgt den Täter. = Policija vajā vainīgo."
        },
        {
          "word": "gehorchen",
          "meaning": "Listen / obey",
          "example": "Das Kind gehorcht. = Bērns klausa."
        },
        {
          "word": "befolgen",
          "meaning": "Follow the instruction",
          "example": "Befolgen Sie die Regeln. = Ievērojiet noteikumus."
        }
      ],
      "tip": [
        "If you can say \"to follow someone\", German often uses folgen with the dative.",
        "If the idea is to 'obey parents' or 'obey orders', gehorchen or befolgen is often more accurate."
      ],
      "important": [
        "folgen = sekot.",
        "Aus etwas folgt ... = it follows from something ...",
        "gehorchen = listen / obey.",
        "folgen requires the dative: ich folge dir."
      ],
