      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: hängen means to hang or hang something on a wall, door, or other place.",
        "If the thing itself is on the wall or on a hook, in English it is usually said to hang.",
        "If a person puts something on a wall, on a hook or in a closet, hängen means hang or hang.",
        "In German, a single form can describe both a state and an action.",
        "The context shows whether the picture is hanging on the wall or someone is hanging it there."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Das Bild hängt an der Wand.",
          "lv": "The picture hangs on the wall."
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich hänge die Jacke in den Schrank.",
          "lv": "I hang the jacket in the closet."
        },
        {
          "de": "Die Lampe hängt über dem Tisch.",
          "lv": "A lamp hangs above the table."
        },
        {
          "de": "Häng den Mantel bitte an den Haken.",
          "lv": "Please hang your coat on the hook."
        },
        {
          "de": "Der Schlüssel hängt neben der Tür.",
          "lv": "The key hangs on the door."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "hängen",
          "meaning": "Hang / order",
          "example": "Das Bild hängt an der Wand. = Attēls karājas pie sienas."
        },
        {
          "word": "stellen",
          "meaning": "Put upright",
          "example": "Ich stelle die Flasche auf den Tisch. = Es nolieku pudeli uz galda."
        },
        {
          "word": "legen",
          "meaning": "To lay down",
          "example": "Ich lege das Buch auf den Tisch. = Es nolieku grāmatu uz galda."
        },
        {
          "word": "an die Wand hängen",
          "meaning": "Hang on the wall",
          "example": "Wir hängen das Bild an die Wand. = Mēs piekaram attēlu pie sienas."
        }
      ],
      "tip": [
        "If the object is on a wall, on a hook or in a closet, hängen is often used.",
        "If the object is placed on the table, compare stellen or legen."
      ],
      "important": [
        "hängen is not a general word meaning to put down.",
        "Stand up with stellen, lie down with legen, and hang with hängen."
      ],
