      "translation": "Comb",
      "explanation": "Der Kamm most often means comb. Less often, it can mean a rooster sext. In the context of a mountain or a roof, Kamm can mean choir. These rarer meanings are usually only clear from context. In everyday life, der Kamm almost always means comb.",
